WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.240
Welcome To FurTuner

2
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:07.440
In this video we will guide you through the steps to create a balanced diet for your pet

3
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.880
Select start to create beginning your pet's diet

4
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.559
Choose your pet type

5
00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:16.160
Choose the type of diet

6
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:23.600
Enter your pets information

7
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:27.680
You can now begin selecting the food ingredients for your recipe

8
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:33.840
Some ingredients group are mandatory, shown in blue while others are optional shown in orange

9
00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.600
each group has a minimum and maximum number of ingredients that you can select

10
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:47.920
For example you must select at least one meat ingredient from this group but you may select up to 3

11
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.320
the optional groups have a maximum number of ingredients that can be selected if you choose to

12
00:00:54.320 --> 00:01:01.199
Scroll through and choose the rest of the ingredients for your recipe

13
00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:05.920
The blue ingredients are the foods you selected for your recipe

14
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:14.240
Depending on your selection, FurTuner may also include some additional balancing ingredients from this orange list

15
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:22.080
These ingredients are used when needed to help ensure that the final diet is complete and balanced

16
00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:38.400
This table displays the complete nutritional profile of the diet including total energy, protein percentage, fat percentage, essential amino acids, essential fatty acids, minerals and vitamins

17
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:47.119
Here under the status you will be able to see whether each nutrient meets or exceeds the minimum AAFCO requirements

18
00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:56.320
If you are satisfied with your diet you can proceed to payment

19
00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:03.439
Once payment has been completed your final recipe will be available to print or email to you

20
00:02:03.439 --> 00:02:12.239
The recipe will contain the amounts of each ingredient in grams and you will have a recipe for one day and up to 30 days

21
00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:17.280
Your printed report will also include the nutritional profile of the diet

22
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.220
The report will also include instructions for preparing the diet

